[repo-allocation name=cx-repos
  [doc [#
THE REPO ALLOCATION — every tracked path in this tree, assigned to the
repository it moves to under the approved multi-repo shape (#1589, the owner
approved the shape 2026-09-21; the execution tracker is #1591). This file is
the allocation as DATA; scripts/repos_allocation_gate.cx is the check that
every tracked file lands in exactly one repo and that no rule here is dead.
It is what each extraction's history filter consumes, and it is the #1077
lesson — enumerate every artifact dimension before anything moves — made
executable.

Nothing here carries a `RULED:` id yet: the decision page superseding
cx_partition.md §5/§5.1 is item 5 on #1591. Until it lands this file states
the plan, and the gate keeps the plan total over the tree.

TWO KINDS OF ROW.
  [repo name= group= ring= ships= about= status=? at=? pins=? vmodule=? why=?]
      one row per destination repository. `group` is the front-page group
      (core | platform | binding | ecosystem | dist), `ring` is 0, 1 or none,
      `ships` is how the repo reaches a user (binary | package | pypi | crate |
      go-module | v-module | editor | none | archived).
      `status=extracted` says the extraction is DONE (RULED: RS-12): the
      repository exists, it owns its paths, and none of them is tracked here
      any more -- so the row carries no `[path]` rules, `at=` records the sha
      `cx` pins it at in deps.cxd, and the gate exempts it from the empty-repo
      refusal while adding the converse one (a `status=extracted` repo that is
      still the first match for a tracked file is an extraction stopped half
      way). Absent `status` means the plan is still a plan.
      `pins='<repo> ...'` and `vmodule=<m>` are the V products' import
      graph (RULED: RS-24, owner D28a): `pins` is the Pins column of the
      #1589 table -- the repositories this one builds on, acyclic -- and
      `vmodule` names the V module the repository compiles from `vcx/<m>/`
      (D31a: flat). A product row gains `vmodule` in the commit that splits
      it. xap's split made xap `vcx/xap/` (`module xap`, the composer with
      it); fabric's split, the last, emptied `vcx/platform/` (`module platform`,
      the RESIDUE the not-yet-split products shared) and xap's PHASE B retired
      it with its catch-all rule. scripts/product_import_gate.cx holds every import under a
      vmodule directory to these pins; the rings (the `core` rows) are always
      importable.
  [path prefix= repo=]  /  [path exact= repo=]
      one allocation rule. A tracked file belongs to the FIRST rule, in
      document order, whose `exact` equals the path or whose `prefix` is a
      leading substring of it. Specific rules are therefore written ABOVE
      general ones; the gate refuses a rule that matches no file, which is how
      a shadowed or stale rule is caught.

HOW TO READ A DECISION HERE. Where a module's repo is not the obvious one,
the rule carries a `why=`. The recurring reasons, once:
  - split by PRODUCT, not by dependency graph (owner, 2026-09-21);
  - the ring membership test (cx_partition.md §10): a module that imports
    nothing and opens no socket is Ring 1 and lives with the language —
    did, vc, authz, bus, the xsp frame codec, iowatch;
  - a shared codec stays in the language repo: saml/scim/oidc/soap/graphql/
    ws/email/http-client have callers outside the one product;
  - a module whose only consumer is one product moves to that product:
    ft → store (the CX-level surface; its V half is cx-core-code's, RULED:
    D84a -- a two-repo module like sasl), sasl → mail, diagram → tooling (the
    CX-level surface; its V half is cx-core-code's, RULED: D78a -- a two-repo
    module like ft);
  - the store owns engine, streams (journal/live/audit) AND server, as
    Postgres does; the session module sits above it in identity;
  - `scripts/`, `tools/`, `docs*/`, `bench/`, `examples/` and the root files
    are the build, release, site and evidence machinery of the whole — they
    go to `cx`, the distribution repo; `_gate_evidence/`, `.claude/`,
    `AGENT-STANDING-RULES.md` and `CLAUDE.md` go to `cx-private`, which stays
    the private orchestration repository (RULED: D59a, D82a) — and each is
    re-homed per repo as each extraction lands (a repo takes its own gates
    with it).
#]]

  [; ── the destinations ─────────────────────────────────────────────── ]
  [repo name=cx group=dist ring=none ships=binary about='the front door: pins every repo, builds the four cx builds and libcx-core/libcx, holds the site, the release, the installer']
  [repo name=cx-private group=dist ring=none ships=none about='the private orchestration repository: boards, evidence, runner configuration, briefs' why='STAYS PRIVATE (RULED: D59a, D82a): the split's own repository, never mirrored public; it holds exactly the paths the public `cx` does not take -- `_gate_evidence/` (runner evidence), `.claude/` (per-tool scaffolding), `AGENT-STANDING-RULES.md` and `CLAUDE.md` (the agent entry points), and `flows/` (the integrator protocol as flow documents with their acts, worlds and `flows/private.mk`, RULED: RFLOW-1 L96, PRIVMK-1 -- the one shared idioms module `flows/ci-acts.cx` and the release document go public by their own rules, and the one gate `scripts/ci_flow_gate.cx` is public so the public documents grade in `cx`) -- while `ledger/` and `spec/03-approved/process/` go public with `cx` (D82a: `spec-freeze-gate` and `cxer-registry-gate` read them at HEAD in `cx`\'s own gate). `cx` is refreshed from this tree\'s green heads by the extraction filter (D83a); this row itself owns no `[path]` rule beyond the six named above, each below']
  [repo name=cx-core-data group=core ring=0 ships=binary status=extracted at=112bc605d8aacb469a3ced4cb55d973d1c82aa6d about='the data format: reader, writer, canonical form, schema, codecs, libcx-core, the data-only cx' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-7, RS-12, D68a), the first V repository: deps.cxd pins it with a v-fork, its V modules (cx, cli, fixtures, arrow, cmd_data, the re2 shim, and since D56a grading -- the corpus grading cores and the cx corpus body both profiles run) are compiled from deps/cx-core-data/vcx through -path, and its data-language corpus and fixtures are graded from the pin. It owns no tracked path here any more: the 87 allotted files this tree grades, builds or documents are re-allocated by D68a to cx and cx-core-code in the block below, each with its reason, and their copies left the repository at the sha at= records. ADVIS-1 (RULED: QUAL-1 (b)): at= is impl/advis1 -- every advisory case names the open issue its red is tracked by (issue=), pushed to cx-home/cx-core-data, not yet merged to main (RS-8). ORDK-1 (RULED: ORDK-1): at= is impl/ordk1 -- the program parser reads the [order-by] keys in one clause and refuses a second clause by name -- pushed to cx-home/cx-core-data, not yet merged to main (RS-8). BATCHH1 (cx-private#1636; RULED: RS-31 -- D70a1 (b)): at= is impl/batchh1 on main a78225565 -- grading/verb.v refuses by name a file whose program case carries a section the program lane does not read, a section twice, two value channels or a case attribute the loader does not read (REFUTE-1), pushed to cx-home/cx-core-data, not yet merged to main (RS-8). Batch H2 (#1648, RULED: FIX-1): at= is impl/batchh2 on main 7ac737d69 -- the program reader asks the [L25c] top-level-comma question once per element body, so cx fmt is linear in the record count, pushed to cx-home/cx-core-data, not yet merged to main (RS-8) DATA1 (cx-private#1776 bug 1, cx-core-data#22, cx-core-data#26 shape 2): at= is impl/data1 on main e57d89da0 -- a bare exponent word with no mantissa (e-1, e5, 1e) reads as text, not 0.0e0; a positional after [else …] in [?match] is refused at parse; a sigil-free comma slot carrying a quoted item takes the data reader's sequence in the program reader; REFUTE-1: a multi-arm [?match] refuses a positional after its first entry -- pushed to cx-home/cx-core-data, not yet merged to main (RS-8). #1769 (RULED: FIX-1): at= is impl/batchh3 on main 4ec1f7268 -- the canonical writer doubles a literal backslash before a byte it writes as an escape (LF, CR, TAB, a C0 control, DEL, the delimiter), so cx fmt is its own fixed point on a backslash before a newline escape -- pushed to cx-home/cx-core-data, not yet merged to main (RS-8)']
  [repo name=cx-core-code group=core ring=1 ships=binary status=extracted at=7823f526acc0d869752c15641ac13bb91a41a46e pins='cx-core-data' about='the language: evaluator, stdlib, LSP, libcx, the cli and embed builds' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-7, D68a, D79a; #1591 item K7a), the second V repository: deps.cxd pins it with a v-fork through cx-core-data (Ring 1 imports Ring 0\'s reader/writer), its V modules (code, cmd, the wasm build, the C ABI, the fixtures grader) compile from deps/cx-core-code/vcx through -path, and the whole Ring-1 stdlib\'s spec/corpus/source not otherwise allotted to a platform product are graded from the pin. It owns no tracked path here any more: vcx/tests/reader_parity_test.v is the one D68a-precedent exception (K7a LETTER, settled) -- it grades examples/ and scripts/, both repo=cx, so it stays TRACKED here instead of moving with the language suite it sits beside. cx-home/cx-core-code main is 896dffd34a (pushed for real; D91a, #1591 item K14 -- vcx/Makefile takes a CX_STAMP_ROOT variable for CX_COMMIT and adds CX_CORE_COMMIT, vcx/cmd/main.v prints the core line beside V fork, fixture-first in vcx/tests/version_stamp_printer_test.v). SITE-1: re2-static now passes CXX=c++ CXXFLAGS="-O3 -g -fPIC -std=c++17" so the public GitHub macOS runner\'s bare clang accepts this re2 vendor snapshot\'s [[clang::fallthrough]] and uniform-init syntax (run 36362512638). DEPSV-1: the deps row in vcx/cmd/main.v (cx deps sync, whose body is the front door\'s vcx/cmd/deps.v) and its fixture in vcx/tests/cli_umbrella_test.v; at= is impl/depsv1 then impl/cx-F-docs4-w5 (the twelve stdlib/cx cases the guide cites, DOCS-47) then impl/cx-F-docs4-w5b (the seventy-two code.cxd cases the data and code pages cite, DOCS-47), pushed to cx-home/cx-core-code, not yet merged to main (RS-8). SETB-1, SETM-1, MEXA-1: at= is impl/setmath -- the cx-stdlib/set module (stdlib/set.cx, vcx/code/stdlib_set.v, its spec and corpus) and math's exact sign/round/truncate/clamp/gcd, pushed to cx-home/cx-core-code, not yet merged to main (RS-8). 1430-e (#1458): at= is impl/kitw1b on main f67ac75f -- security.md section 2.1\'s cx-platform/ftp effect points and the bundle\'s ftp arm, prepared in the mover\'s clone and named by sha in _gate_evidence/pipeline_kitw1b/RESULTS.md (RS-8). TIMEP-1: at= is impl/timep rebased onto main 851dcfc1b -- the time module splits by effect, its clock-free half in every profile and only the clock reads its pack -- pushed to cx-home/cx-core-code, not yet merged to main (RS-8). ADVIS-1 (RULED: QUAL-1 (b)): at= is impl/advis1 -- every advisory case names the open issue its red is tracked by (issue=), pushed to cx-home/cx-core-code, not yet merged to main (RS-8). ORDK-1 (RULED: ORDK-1): at= is impl/ordk1 -- [order-by] takes its keys in one clause, each with its own direction, a second clause refused by name -- pushed to cx-home/cx-core-code, not yet merged to main (RS-8). BATCHH1 (cx-private#1623 and cx-private#1636): at= is impl/batchh1 on main d98c5dd66 -- streamed_for_alloc_probe.v compiles again (rung 7 boxes its LazyRecord through cx.mk_lazy_record), the corpus_verb fixtures of the vocabulary refusal of the program lane and of REFUTE-1, and code.cxd program-tree-eval-nonwidening-001/002 carrying grant=eval on the case instead of a [grant eval] child no grader read, pushed to cx-home/cx-core-code, not yet merged to main (RS-8). CORE1 (RULED: TDUR-1, TMPD-1): at= is impl/core1 -- time's duration verbs answer the duration scalar, the io temp surface honours TMPDIR, a [bus] is single-owner and reads its topic-of option -- pushed to cx-home/cx-core-code, not yet merged to main (RS-8) DATA1 (cx-core-data#22): at= is impl/data1 on main b868494bf -- code.cxd program-match-multi-023 (a positional after [else …] refuses) leaves advisory, program-match-multi-024 (after the last [case …]) added, and cxparse_full_corpus_diff_test's baseline moves by the round's ten in-cx inputs, pushed to cx-home/cx-core-code, not yet merged to main (RS-8). Issue 1769 (RULED: FIX-1): at= is impl/batchh3 on main 1701e1235 -- the cxparse differential baseline moves with the eight new in-cx inputs of cx-core-data impl/batchh3 (total 1290, agree 995, diverge 114) -- pushed to cx-home/cx-core-code, not yet merged to main (RS-8)']
  [repo name=cx-platform-net group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=cxnet status=extracted at=d2104276466ed0093e42dc1064074c6405c82e2a pins='cx-core-code' about='sockets, TLS, the HTTP server, the XSP transport bindings, ftp, sftp, file_surface' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-24, #1591 item 20), the third V product (after core-data): its own vcx/cxnet/ (module cxnet) and vcx/transport/ leave with it. It owns no tracked path here any more; cx reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha at= records, and registry/modules.cxd\'s http, net, ftp and sftp rows -- plus the file_surface catalog row -- name the pinned checkout. KEY-1 (RULED: D59a): h2_localhost_{cert,key}.pem now generates at run time; at= is impl/key1-loopback-pair, not yet pushed (RS-8)']
  [repo name=cx-platform-mail group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=mail status=extracted at=7248839d048925940174d84b26b337a6c786a8c9 pins='cx-platform-net' about='SMTP and IMAP, server and client cores, sasl' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-19, D71a, D76c; #1591 item 20): its V module vcx/mail/ (module mail) compiles from deps/cx-platform-mail/vcx through -path and its spec, corpus and source are graded from the pin. The four files that stayed until D71a -- the declared pure halves of imap and smtp, once called INTRA-MODULE by vcx/code/stdlib_dispatch.v -- left with the builtin-dispatch registration hook: code exposes register_stdlib_builtin and mail\'s own init() registers smtp and imap. sasl\'s V dispatch, vcx/code/stdlib_sasl.v, is the core\'s (D76c: Ring 1 and pure), while its spec, corpus and source stay here. It owns no tracked path here any more; cx reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha at= records, and registry/modules.cxd\'s sasl, imap and smtp rows name the pinned checkout Since #1657 smtp and imap serve hand their accept thread code\'s MatchEnv.spawn_env() instead of the caller\'s stack env. KEY-1 (RULED: D59a): the committed h2_localhost_{cert,key}.pem is gone; at= is impl/key1-loopback-pair, not yet pushed (RS-8)']
  [repo name=cx-platform-identity group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=identity pins='cx-platform-store cx-platform-net cx-platform-xsp' status=extracted at=748f0d736fcab83300ef0d1b455f7d2981fab8ee about='sessions, did:web, authz-store, vc-revocation' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8, D65d; #1591 item K3): deps.cxd pins it with a v-fork -- its V module (vcx/identity/, module identity) compiles from deps/cx-platform-identity/vcx through -path, and its session/authz-store/did-web/vc-revocation spec/corpus/source are graded from the pin. The one file that stayed until D65d, vcx/code/stdlib_xsp_auth.v (xsp-auth\'s declared Ring-1 half), left for cx-platform-xsp with the rest of cx-platform/xsp-auth (its registration, source, spec and corpus left this repository\'s own tree in the same commit), so it owns no tracked path here any more. The commit at= records is NOT YET PUSHED to cx-home/cx-platform-identity (component-repo pushes are the integrator\'s, RS-8; it is prepared in the mover\'s clone and named by sha in _gate_evidence/pipeline_xxsp/RESULTS.md)']
  [repo name=cx-platform-store group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=store pins='cx-core-code cx-platform-net cx-platform-xsp' status=extracted at=39c433f8057fa5136dca3fe611bbeca5e8583627 about='the storage engine, its substrates, journal/live/audit, ft, and the store server' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8, D71a, D73a, D84a; #1591 item K3): the RS-24 vcx/store/ split (module store) already stood alone from vcx/platform/, so extraction moved it, vcx/cxstore/ and vcx/cmd/store_ whole out -- store\'s, journal\'s, live\'s and audit\'s spec, corpus and source now name deps/cx-platform-store/ in registry/modules.cxd, and so does ft\'s CX-level surface (stdlib/ft.cx, its spec, its corpus), even though ft is a Ring-1 cx-stdlib module the store repository merely carries as its only consumer. The one file that stayed, vcx/code/stdlib_ft.v (ft\'s V dispatch half), RE-ALLOCATES to cx-core-code under D84a: it is Ring 1 and pure and the ring decides where a module lives (D76c) -- code\'s stdlib_dispatch.v and both of eval.v\'s env chains keep calling it as a same-module function, so no env-aware hook is built. It owns no tracked path here any more. The three vcx/cmd/store_{serve,rotate,principal}_d_cx_platform.v files that stayed with it left under D73a: code exposes register_cli_verb and the store\'s own init() registers store-serve, store-health, store-rotate-kek and store-mint-principal into cmd\'s verb table. Since D65d the store\'s XSP connections import the XSP-AUTH calculus from cx-platform-xsp (module xsp), which it pins; that commit, at= above, is NOT YET PUSHED (RS-8; named in _gate_evidence/pipeline_xxsp/RESULTS.md)']
  [repo name=cx-platform-db group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=cxdb pins='cx-core-code' status=extracted at=2cad4457b081f1929fbe79609947dc1aa6ca9aa3 about='external database access: $sql-*, $redis-*, the drivers' why='at= moves again here (RULED: DBSRV-1, CXF-8) -- tooling/db_real.cx\'s `remove` now runs `docker rm -f -v` so the forced removal also reclaims the per-server anonymous data volume a bare `docker rm -f` left behind (137 of them, 18.02 GB, filled colima\'s 20 GiB disk, cx-platform-db#6, DBVOL-1); tooling/db_real_selftest.cx\'s fixture proves `docker volume ls -q` is unchanged by a real start+remove and that the vanished-container message names the exit the daemon still has, never a bare "No such container"; at= moves here for kit wave 1C (RULED: 1455-a; cx-private #1459): db_access.md §2.1, the backend registry as an open row set (four current rows, seven planned), and the ENGINE=FILE arguments of tooling/db_real.cx, through which test-db-real grades the kind=db cases of the connector kit on the same servers. EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8; #1591 item K3), a V product: the RS-24 vcx/cxdb/ split (module cxdb) already stood alone from vcx/platform/, so extraction moved it out whole -- the sql, redis and db rows of registry/modules.cxd now name their spec, corpus and code under deps/cx-platform-db/, and xap (its only in-tree consumer, per its own pins=) reaches the dispatch registration through the pin, not a tracked path. It has no [path] rules any more; `cx` reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha `at=` records. `at=` moves again here (RULED: DBSPEC-1, WORDS-1) -- db_access.md truing outside section 7.1 for the real-server step, and the word "lane" leaving cx-platform-db (RULED: RUN-2, RS-12, RS-8; #1591 item K3) -- connector_live_test.v read reference/acme/ from cx-private's own root, gone with xap's extraction; a prepared fix commit (mover's clone, NOT PUSHED, RS-8) reads it from the cx-platform-xap pin instead. ADVIS-1 (RULED: QUAL-1 (b)): at= is impl/advis1 -- every advisory case names the open issue its red is tracked by (issue=), pushed to cx-home/cx-platform-db, not yet merged to main (RS-8)']
  [repo name=cx-platform-fabric group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=fabric pins='cx-platform-store cx-platform-identity cx-platform-net cx-platform-xsp' status=extracted at=cbe72fbbbf79e994ddbc3652b592bba7a9766c14 about='messaging and fabric-serve' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8, D73a; #1591 item K3): its V module vcx/fabric/ (module fabric) compiles from deps/cx-platform-fabric/vcx through -path and its spec, corpus and source are graded from the pin. vcx/cmd/fabric_serve_d_cx_platform.v left through the CLI-verb-registry hook D73a already gives cx-platform-store: code exposes register_cli_verb and fabric\'s own init() registers fabric-serve into cmd\'s verb table. NOT YET PUSHED to cx-home/cx-platform-fabric (component-repo pushes are the integrator\'s, RS-8; the commit is prepared in the mover\'s clone and named by sha in RESULTS.md, per the K3 brief). Since D65d fabric-serve and the remote tier import the XSP-AUTH calculus from cx-platform-xsp (module xsp), which it pins, and the pre-move copy of fabric-serve the catch-up left in its vcx/cmd/ is gone; those two commits, at= above, are likewise NOT YET PUSHED (_gate_evidence/pipeline_xxsp/RESULTS.md). It owns no tracked path here any more; cx reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha `at=` records. XAP2 (#1650): at= is impl/xap2 -- the remote handle's receive and serve pumps hold its mutex one read tick at a time and yield it to waiting verbs, fixture-first in vcx/tests/fabric_umbrella_test.v, pushed to cx-home/cx-platform-fabric, not yet merged to main (RS-8). XAP3 (#1771): at= is impl/xap3 -- the remote handle is a frame router: each pull is bounded by its own deadline, a responder callable runs with no lock held, a request is answered by its own handle's serve pump, fixture-first in vcx/tests/fabric_umbrella_test.v, pushed to cx-home/cx-platform-fabric, not yet merged to main (RS-8)']
  [repo name=cx-platform-xsp group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=xsp pins='cx-core-code' status=extracted at=6b6f152609721d5e3923083accb6bd115a5e3044 about='the XAP Stream Protocol: the frame codec, the XSP-AUTH handshake, the protocol pages' why='EXTRACTED (RULED: D65d, RS-31, RS-24, RS-12): XSP is a PRODUCT, used across the platform (D65d amends RS-2, RS-3 and RS-15). Its V module vcx/xsp/ (module xsp: the pure XSP-AUTH calculus that sat in vcx/code as xsp-auth\'s declared half, and its registration, identity\'s until D65d) compiles from deps/cx-platform-xsp/vcx through -path and imports only code and cx, so its only pin is cx-core-code; the store, identity, fabric and xap pin it and reach the calculus through import xsp. cx-platform/xsp-auth\'s source, spec and corpus and cx-stdlib/xsp\'s source, catalog page, corpus and the protocol page (spec/03-approved/xap/xsp.md) are graded from the pin; cx-stdlib/xsp\'s V dispatch, vcx/code/stdlib_xsp.v, stays cx-core-code\'s (Ring 1 and pure: the ring decides where code lives, D76c). D65d names cx-platform-net among its pins for the push-down surface over its connections; nothing imports net yet, so the pin waits for the first import. NOT YET PUSHED to cx-home/cx-platform-xsp, which does not exist yet (the integrator creates and pushes it, RS-8; the commits are prepared in the mover\'s clone and named in _gate_evidence/pipeline_xxsp/RESULTS.md). It owns no tracked path here any more; cx reaches it through deps.cxd, which pins it at the sha at= records']
  [repo name=cx-platform-xap group=platform ring=none ships=binary vmodule=xap status=extracted pins='cx-platform-net cx-platform-mail cx-platform-identity cx-platform-store cx-platform-db cx-platform-fabric cx-platform-xsp' at=80a913a896b67eb6b8fff9840a9d492585981e58 about='the application host, compose, dist, schema, market, the reference deployments' why="PARTLY EXTRACTED (RULED: RS-12, RS-8, RS-7, RS-20; #1591 item K3): deps.cxd pins it with a v-fork -- git-init'd + two commits (a skeleton, then the catch-up at this repository's own head), not filter-repo (no history to carry). cx-home/cx-platform-xap's main is 87a10940c (the integrator's push of the mover's first two corrections: dropping seven module-main files a prefix match misallocated, named below, then dropping examples/platform/together/ -- the sso-flow-xap multi-repo demo and its README -- the #1536 precedent's shape when sso left applied here too); this row's at= is a THIRD correction on top, NOT YET PUSHED (the integrator pushes it, RS-8): D77 (owner ruling (d), 2026-09-24) -- a minimal registry-store fixture of xap's own (conformance/xap/fixtures/registry-store/, gtin@0.1.0) replaces the read of cx-registry's checkout the four xap-dist cases never pinned; `make corpus` there is 246/246 (223 enforced + 23 xap-schema advisory-red, unchanged). Its V module (vcx/xap/, module xap: the composer, coordination incl. the flow-perform seam, dist, the contract revision) compiles from deps/cx-platform-xap/vcx through -path, and xap's spec/corpus/source (spec/03-approved/xap/ and the platform catalog remainder, conformance/xap/, stdlib/xap.cx), market/, packages/ (the gtin sample), reference/, examples/htmx/ and examples/platform/xap/, bench/xap/ and its three xap-named scripts are graded from the pin. Since D65d the composer (vcx/xap/ring2_register.v) and the host's two auth files import the XSP-AUTH calculus from cx-platform-xsp (module xsp), which it pins; that commit, on top of 3c30c52, is the at= above and is NOT YET PUSHED (_gate_evidence/pipeline_xxsp/RESULTS.md) -- that correction is a pin-sha matter, tracked separately from path ownership. K7c (RULED: D68a, D59a/RS-28, RS-12; 2026-09-25) re-allocates the seven files that used to stay here -- vcx/cmd/xap_{check_surface,compat,init,init_templates,scaffold,scaffold_templates}.v and platform_verbs_d_cx_platform.v, all `module main`, called intra-module from vcx/cmd/main.v's plain (non-platform-gated) subcommands list, only compiled by the front door through sync-cmd-split -- to repo=cx below; this row now owns no tracked path here at all, so it takes status=extracted for that reason, independent of the at= correction's push. ADVIS-1 (RULED: QUAL-1 (b)): at= is impl/advis1 -- the xap-schema suite element names the open issue its advisory reds are tracked by (issue=), pushed to cx-home/cx-platform-xap, not yet merged to main (RS-8). XAP2 (#1727): at= is impl/xap2 -- the [xap-runtime] carries the closeable contract (xap.md §4.7), fixture-first in conformance/xap/xap-serve.cxd (xap-runtime-close-001…005), pushed to cx-home/cx-platform-xap, not yet merged to main (RS-8). XAP3 (#1772): at= is impl/xap3 -- every verb answers a closed runtime CXER4859 at one entry check, and a non-blocking host runtime is closeable, fixture-first (xap-runtime-close-006…009 enforced; two V cases in vcx/tests/xap_umbrella_test.v, whose delegations guards now read their directories from the pin and whose probes read either spelling of a printed value, green whole under test-xap-umbrella), pushed to cx-home/cx-platform-xap, not yet merged to main (RS-8)"]
