as no asset-only pin shape for a non-module repository, so there is no pinned successor to retarget either reader at). The re-allocation rules are below, each carrying this paragraph\'s reasoning; this row itself now carries no [path] rule at all. BATCHH1 (cx-private#1632; RULED: RS-7): at= is impl/batchh1 -- its make check runs the own gate of the ledger (ledger-index-selftest, ledger-index-check) with the indexer pinned from cx (deps/cx-private/scripts/ledger_index.cx; scripts/ stays in cx, no allocation change) over its own ledger/ and its own subjects (a blank history refused, REFUTE-1), and its ledger/ brought to the bytes of 8b63de0c7, pushed to cx-home/cx-decisions, not yet merged to main (RS-8)']
